{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1488585-is-vidal-still-the-prince-of-new-orleans-2nd-edition","id":1488585,"title":"Is Vidal still the Prince of New Orleans 2nd edition ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-31T11:18:12-07:00","id":1488585,"title":"Is Vidal still the Prince of New Orleans 2nd edition ?","content":"Just curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T11:57:10-07:00","id":1488590,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, Chronicles avoids doing metaplot things, so Vidal is still the Prince in canon materials.<br /> <br /> (Hunter has mildly flirted with that, and the general response to that was not positive, so.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T13:12:05-07:00","id":1488595,"title":"","content":"He is, but since the First Edition, he has... Gone through some things.<br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum part of <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/199280/Secrets-of-the-Covenants?src=hottest_filtered\" target=\"_blank\">Secrets of the Covenants</a> is told mostly from his point of view. Since the first book, his domain was devastated by Katrina, and Anton Savoy was eliminated. Baron Cimitere is still undead, but he's also lost a lot of, if not most of his mortal followers. Of course, Vidal lost a lot of allies, subjects, and assets in the destruction too, and he's convinced Hurricane Katrina was some punishment from God, rather than, you know, a natural disaster that was possibly exacerbated by climate change.<br /> <br /> Now Vidal's New Orleans is under siege from a Carthian invasion, but an odd one. They're mostly from Houston where the Movement has blended with the Lancea Sanctum of all people. There is a little more info about them in the Carthian section.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, he has been taking the past decade and a half VERY poorly, and his part of the book ends with the implication he's about to go full Torquemada, purging the Carthians and everybody else that has pissed him off, which makes up for a LOT of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 07-31-2022, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"